    "title": "Celebrity chefs face off for best chili award - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Lindsey Watson ,\n2 hours ago\nBEAVER TWP., Ohio (WKBN) – The results are in for this year’s annual Chili Cookoff, hosted by the Boardman Optimist Club.\nMore than a dozen celebrity chefs served up their secret recipes for votes Wednesday night at Avion on the Water in Beaver Township.\nFirst News anchor Lindsey Watson served as emcee for the fifth year in a row.\nThis year’s competition was close, and it got heated.\nIn the Battle of the Broadcasters, First News reporter Jeremy Jones took home the top prize. He was up against First News This Morning Meteorologist Hanna Erdmann.\nAll of the money raised goes back to the Optimist Club to invest in various local programs, benefiting children in the community.\n“It’s really something. It’s our sole fundraiser for the year, and the cooks, the local politicians come out every year and support us — some of them for 10 to 15 years now, so we really appreciate it,” said Chuck Hillman, of the Boardman Optimist Club.\nThis year’s event was so crowded that several cooks ran out of chili within the first hour and a half.\nThe winners are as follows:\nHottest chili: Michael Rulli\nMost original chili- Tom McCabe\nFavorite political chili- Geno DeFabio\nFavorite celebrity {battle of the broadcasters} – Jeremy Jones\nBest of the chili cookoff – Anthony Traficanti\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKBN.com.",
